      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "islam_is_the_religion_of_peace",
      "label": "Claim about Islam being a religion of peace",
      "description": "This phrase is a common religious and political statement used to describe Islam as a peaceful faith. It is often used in interfaith dialogue, by Muslim communities, and by advocates for religious tolerance. However, in the context of this meme, it is juxtaposed with hateful text to create a false or ironic contrast, implying that the peaceful image contradicts the violent message, which is a manipulative tactic often used in Islamophobic rhetoric.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2b5f4964"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9b30373a",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "piece_of_you_over_here_piece_of_you_over_there",
      "label": "Derogatory phrase implying fragmentation or elimination",
      "description": "This phrase is a violent, dehumanizing metaphor often used in hate speech to describe Muslims or people of Islamic faith. It implies that they are fragmented, dangerous, or should be separated or eliminated. The phrase is rooted in Islamophobic stereotypes that portray Muslims as inherently violent or chaotic, and it is used to incite fear and hatred. It is not a literal or neutral expression but a hateful trope.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
